Rainer Schoepf writes on the name `NFSS';

> However, with LaTeX2e we are carrying the name to the wide world for
> the very first time.

This seems to me to be exactly the point of this discussion. Within LaTeX2e
there will be no notion of an `old' font selection scheme, just a LaTeX2.09
compatability mode. Therefore we dont *need* a name for the font selection
schemes, other than the name of the LaTeX versions in which they are default.
So lets drop references to `NFSS' when talking about LaTeX2e.

Dean

